<AdditionalHelpText>
<![CDATA[Copyright © Rockwell Automation, Inc.  All Rights Reserved.

This instruction calculates the Gross Observed Volume (GOV) of Product in
an upright cylindrical tank, given:

    Input: Overall Level (Innage, from bottom ref.) (typ. Product + Free Water
      - see below)
    Configuration: Tank Calibration Table (array with volume at given level)
        (also called a Strapping Table, hence the instruction name)

If optional Free Water adjusment is selected, the following are required:

    Input: Interface Innage Level (level of Free Water only)

If optional Compensation for Thermal Expansion of the tank shell
is selected, the following are required:

    Input: Average Product Temperature  (suggestion: use P_AInMulti ! )
    Input: Ambient Temperature (if tank is not insulated)
    Configuration: "K" factor (weighting of product vs ambient)
       (enter zero for this configuration if tank is insulated)
    Configuration: Linear Coefficient of Thermal Expansion for tank shell material of construction
    Configuration:  Reference Temperature for tank calibration table (typ. 60 Deg F or 15 Deg C)

If optional Floating Roof Adjustment is selected, the following are required:

    Input:  Obesrved Density (Deg API) at PRODUCT Temperature
    Configuration:  Reference Density (typ. 35 API)
    Configuration:  Correction Volume per API (typ. a negative number)
    Configuration:  Level at which to start FRA (level above which roof floats)

The Gross Observed Volume (GOV) and intermediates are provided as Values:
    Val_TOV:  Total Observed Volume
    Val_FW:    Free Water Volume
    Val_CTSh:  Correction for Temperature of Tank Shell (multiplier)
    Val_FRA:   Floating Roof Adjustment (volume)
    Val_GOV:  Primary Value: Gross Observed Volume

Val_GOV is provided without correction for product temperautre, density,
included sediment and water (BS&W).  Those corrections depend on the
product, not the tank, and are beyond the scope of this instruction.

References:  API MPMS 2.2A, API MPMS 12.1.1;  see www.api.org
for more information.
]]>
</AdditionalHelpText>
<Parameters>
